  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Providing Integrated Humanitarian Assistance to Displaced Populations in Iraq &#x2013; Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The humanitarian situation in Iraq continues to be characterized by general instability, protracted internal displacement, lack of public services, as well as inadequate shelter and housing. Humanitarian and protection needs remain significant across the country, despite the discontinuation of the humanitarian cluster system and the transition away from a post-conflict context. In this project, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) continues building on previous and current humanitarian interventions, with a focus on improving the living conditions of displaced families in out-of-camp locations who are prevented or not able to return or integrate locally, through an integrated humanitarian response. IOM is providing shelter assistance and continues to strengthen its response in remote and underserved informal sites. The most critical needs of displaced populations are being addressed through the provision of integrated shelter support and site upgrades to improve safe and dignified living conditions and allow internally displaced families to concentrate on other needs.</narrative>
  </description>
